  "prefLabel": "Ins 4703.07 Prohibited Policy Provisions, Exclusions, and Limitations",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 4703.07 Prohibited Policy Provisions, Exclusions, and Limitations. An inland marine travel insurance policy shall not contain provisions that:\n\n(a) Guarantee policy renewal;\n\n(b) Charge a penalty or administrative fee for trip cancellation by the covered individual;\n\n(c) Retain unearned premium payments when the trip is cancelled or terminated by the group policyholder or its affiliates; or\n\n(d) Reduce coverage based on the age of the insured.\n\nSource. #10681, eff 11-3-14; ss by #13989, eff 5-29-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins4700.html"
}
